SELECT define_provision($q$LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02$q$, $q$Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Road Frontage Boundaries Circumstance (A)(d)-(e), (D), (E)$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || Table SC10.1.1: Setback standards for development located in the Rural Zone or the Emerging Community Zone | Note: The setback standards for the Emerging Community Zone apply where located in an area that is not the subject of a Local Plan, or an approved structure plan area, which has approved documents that vary the effect of the planning scheme with alternative assessment benchmarks for setbacks. | The development is on a lot having an area 0 m2 to 2,999 m2 | The road frontage lot boundary setbacks identified in Circumstance (A) or Circumstance (B) apply to buildings or structures unless the building or structure complies with Circumstance (C), or Circumstance (D), or Circumstance (E). | Circumstance (A): If the lot is not a corner lot, buildings or structures have a setback from road frontage lot boundaries in accordance with the following: (a) a dwelling has a setback of at least three (3) metres; (b) decks, patios, pergolas, verandahs, balconies, gazebos or the like have a setback of at least three (3) metres; (c) a garage forming part of a dwelling has a setback of at least six (6) metres; (d) a standalone Class 10a building under the Building Code of Australia being a shed, garage or carport has a setback of at least six (6) metres; and (e) any other building or structure has a setback of at least six (6) metres. | Circumstance (D): If it is a roofed gatehouse or arch which: (a) has a maximum area of four (4) square metres; and (b) is not more than (2) metres wide to the street; and (c) is not more than three (3) metres in height. | Circumstance (E): A building or structure that: (a) if standalone, does not have an ‘outermost projection height’ exceeding two (2) metres; or (b) if involving a combination with other buildings or structures, does not result in a combined height exceeding two (2) metres. Editor’s note: An example of a ‘combination’ is a fence and a retaining wall or a building and a retaining wall.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$Rural zone code p.P6-89 (PDF p.8); Emerging community zone code p.P6-76 (PDF p.6); Schedule 10 p.SC10-2 to SC10-5 (PDF pp.2-5)$q$, NULL, $q$Rural zone code / Emerging community zone code + Schedule 10$q$, NULL, $q$https://www.livingstone.qld.gov.au/files/sharedassets/public/v/1/doing-business/documents/10_Sch10_Boundary_setbacks_for_zones_V4_Adopted_2025_02_18.pdf$q$, $q$SC1.2 Setback: "the shortest distance, measured horizontally, between the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the boundary of the lot where the building or structure is." Outermost projection excludes a retractable blind, fixed screen, rainwater fitting or ornamental attachment. Outermost projection height is measured to ground level directly below that point.$q$, $q$lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_class10a$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_class10a", "instrument_version": "LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02", "topic": "SETBACK.FRONTAGE", "title": "Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Road Frontage Boundaries Circumstance (A)(d)-(e), (D), (E)", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_FRONT", "operator": ">=", "value": 6, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2025-05-02", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "LIVINGSTONE"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:RURAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:EMERGING_COMMUNITY"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_10A", "CLASS_1"], "sources": [{"key": "lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_class10a", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"lot is not a corner lot\", \"garage forming part of a dwelling: 6 m (not Class 10a standalone but same value)\", \"decks, patios, pergolas, verandahs, balconies, gazebos or the like: 3 m\"], \"exceptions\": [\"open carport / shade sail: see Circumstance (C) rule (posts >= 1 m)\", \"roofed gatehouse or arch <= 4 m2, <= 2 m wide to street, <= 3 m high\", \"building or structure (incl. fence + retaining wall combination) with outermost projection height / combined height not exceeding 2 m\"], \"formula_text\": null, \"parameter\": \"road frontage setback, standalone Class 10a building (shed, garage, carport) and any other building or structure\", \"operator\": \">=\", \"value\": 6}\nLot conditions (not encoded): lots 0 m2 to 2,999 m2\nStructure scope 'a standalone Class 10a building under the Building Code of Australia being a shed, garage or carport; any other building or structure' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A', 'CLASS_1']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - Part 1 s1.6(3): \"This planning scheme, through Part 5, regulates building work in accordance with sections 32 and 33 of the Building Act 1975.\" and s1.6(4)(c) lists \"Relevant zone codes\" (and (e) \"Seaspray Local Plan\") as building assessment provisions; the s1.6 editor's note cites \"alternative boundary clearances and site cover provisions for Class 1 and 10 structures under section 33\". Table 5.6.1 makes standalone Class 10a building work accepted subject to requirements against these AOs.\nResearcher notes: Zone code AO adopts Schedule 10 by reference. Swimming pools, if a 'structure', fall under (e) 'any other building or structure' (6 m) unless under 2 m outermost projection height (in-ground pools likely exempt via Circumstance (E)); scheme does not name pools expressly. For the Emerging Community Zone the table applies only outside a Local Plan or approved structure plan area (table note). In the Rural Zone, AO5.1 applies in all areas excluding the Yaamba Historic Township Precinct (see lsc_rur_yaamba_* rules)."}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_class10a@2025-05-02$q$;
INSERT INTO rule_relationships (from_rule_version_id, to_rule_id, type, basis_provision_id, verification, notes) VALUES ($q$LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_class10a@2025-05-02$q$, $q$QDC12.A1a.ROAD_SETBACK$q$, 'OVERRIDES', p('QLD_BUILDING_ACT_1975@2026-02-01', 's 33'), 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', 'Alternative provision (Building Act s33(4)): QDC applies only to the extent this provision does not. Scope must be confirmed per rule (zone/precinct/structure).');
INSERT INTO rule_relationships (from_rule_version_id, to_rule_id, type, basis_provision_id, verification, notes) VALUES ($q$LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_class10a@2025-05-02$q$, $q$QDC11.A1a.FRONTAGE_SETBACK$q$, 'OVERRIDES', p('QLD_BUILDING_ACT_1975@2026-02-01', 's 33'), 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', 'Alternative provision (Building Act s33(4)): QDC applies only to the extent this provision does not. Scope must be confirmed per rule (zone/precinct/structure).');
SELECT define_provision($q$LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02$q$, $q$Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Road Frontage Boundaries Circumstance (B)$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || Table SC10.1.1: Setback standards for development located in the Rural Zone or the Emerging Community Zone | Note: The setback standards for the Emerging Community Zone apply where located in an area that is not the subject of a Local Plan, or an approved structure plan area, which has approved documents that vary the effect of the planning scheme with alternative assessment benchmarks for setbacks. | The development is on a lot having an area 0 m2 to 2,999 m2 | The road frontage lot boundary setbacks identified in Circumstance (A) or Circumstance (B) apply to buildings or structures unless the building or structure complies with Circumstance (C), or Circumstance (D), or Circumstance (E). | Circumstance (B): If the lot is a corner lot, buildings or structures have a setback from road frontage lot boundaries in accordance with the following: (a) if the ‘depth of a lot’ has an average of greater than twenty-four (24) metres: (i) a dwelling has a setback of at least three (3) metres; (ii) decks, patios, pergolas, verandahs, balconies, gazebos or the like have a setback of at least three (3) metres; (iii) a garage forming part of a dwelling has a setback of at least six (6) metres; (iv) a standalone Class 10a buildings under the Building Code of Australia being a shed, garage or carport has a setback of at least six (6) metres; (v) any other building or structure has a setback of at least six (6) metres; and (vi) despite (a)(i), (a)(ii), (a)(iii), (a)(iv) or (a)(v), no building or structure over two (2) metres high is built on the lot within a nine (9) by nine (9) metre truncation at the corner of two road frontages (refer to Figure SC10.1.5); or (b) if the ‘depth of a lot’ has an average of twenty-four (24) metres or less: (i) for the ‘primary road frontage’: (A) a dwelling has a setback of at least three (3) metres; (B) decks, patios, pergolas, verandahs, balconies, gazebos or the like have a setback of at least three (3) metres; (C) a garage forming part of a dwelling has a setback of at least six (6) metres; (D) a standalone Class 10a buildings under the Building Code of Australia being a shed, garage or carport has a setback of at least six (6) metres; (E) any other building or structure has a setback of at least six (6) metres; and (F) despite (b)(i)(A), (b)(i)(B), (b)(i)(C), (b)(i)(D), or (b)(i)(E), no building or structure over two (2) metres high is built on the lot within a nine (9) by nine (9) metre truncation at the corner of two road frontages (refer to Figure SC10.1.5);$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$Rural zone code p.P6-89 (PDF p.8); Emerging community zone code p.P6-76 (PDF p.6); Schedule 10 p.SC10-2 to SC10-5 (PDF pp.2-5)$q$, NULL, $q$Rural zone code / Emerging community zone code + Schedule 10$q$, NULL, $q$https://www.livingstone.qld.gov.au/files/sharedassets/public/v/1/doing-business/documents/10_Sch10_Boundary_setbacks_for_zones_V4_Adopted_2025_02_18.pdf$q$, $q$SC1.2 Setback: "the shortest distance, measured horizontally, between the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the boundary of the lot where the building or structure is." Outermost projection excludes a retractable blind, fixed screen, rainwater fitting or ornamental attachment. Outermost projection height is measured to ground level directly below that point.$q$, $q$lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_corner_class10a$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_corner_class10a", "instrument_version": "LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02", "topic": "SETBACK.FRONTAGE", "title": "Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Road Frontage Boundaries Circumstance (B)", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_FRONT", "operator": ">=", "value": 6, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2025-05-02", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "LIVINGSTONE"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:RURAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:EMERGING_COMMUNITY"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_10A", "CLASS_1"], "sources": [{"key": "lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_corner_class10a", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"lot is a corner lot\", \"depth of lot average > 24 m: 6 m from road frontage lot boundaries\", \"depth of lot average <= 24 m: 6 m from the 'primary road frontage' (secondary frontage per Figure SC10.1.6 - out of scope)\", \"no building or structure over 2 m high within a 9 m x 9 m truncation at the corner of two road frontages\"], \"exceptions\": [\"Circumstances (C) open carport/shade sail, (D) gatehouse/arch, (E) <= 2 m structures as for non-corner lots\"], \"formula_text\": null, \"parameter\": \"road frontage setback on corner lot (primary road frontage), standalone Class 10a building and any other building or structure\", \"operator\": \">=\", \"value\": 6}\nLot conditions (not encoded): lots 0 m2 to 2,999 m2; corner lots\nStructure scope 'a standalone Class 10a buildings under the Building Code of Australia being a shed, garage or carport; any other building or structure' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A', 'CLASS_1']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - Part 1 s1.6(3): \"This planning scheme, through Part 5, regulates building work in accordance with sections 32 and 33 of the Building Act 1975.\" and s1.6(4)(c) lists \"Relevant zone codes\" (and (e) \"Seaspray Local Plan\") as building assessment provisions; the s1.6 editor's note cites \"alternative boundary clearances and site cover provisions for Class 1 and 10 structures under section 33\". Table 5.6.1 makes standalone Class 10a building work accepted subject to requirements against these AOs.\nResearcher notes: Secondary road frontage limb (b)(ii) omitted (out of scope; refers to Figure SC10.1.6 image). For the Emerging Community Zone the table applies only outside a Local Plan or approved structure plan area (table note). In the Rural Zone, AO5.1 applies in all areas excluding the Yaamba Historic Township Precinct (see lsc_rur_yaamba_* rules)."}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_corner_class10a@2025-05-02$q$;
INSERT INTO rule_relationships (from_rule_version_id, to_rule_id, type, basis_provision_id, verification, notes) VALUES ($q$LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_corner_class10a@2025-05-02$q$, $q$QDC12.A1a.ROAD_SETBACK$q$, 'OVERRIDES', p('QLD_BUILDING_ACT_1975@2026-02-01', 's 33'), 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', 'Alternative provision (Building Act s33(4)): QDC applies only to the extent this provision does not. Scope must be confirmed per rule (zone/precinct/structure).');
INSERT INTO rule_relationships (from_rule_version_id, to_rule_id, type, basis_provision_id, verification, notes) VALUES ($q$LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_corner_class10a@2025-05-02$q$, $q$QDC11.A1a.FRONTAGE_SETBACK$q$, 'OVERRIDES', p('QLD_BUILDING_ACT_1975@2026-02-01', 's 33'), 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', 'Alternative provision (Building Act s33(4)): QDC applies only to the extent this provision does not. Scope must be confirmed per rule (zone/precinct/structure).');
SELECT define_provision($q$LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02$q$, $q$Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Road Frontage Boundaries Circumstance (C)$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || Table SC10.1.1: Setback standards for development located in the Rural Zone or the Emerging Community Zone | Note: The setback standards for the Emerging Community Zone apply where located in an area that is not the subject of a Local Plan, or an approved structure plan area, which has approved documents that vary the effect of the planning scheme with alternative assessment benchmarks for setbacks. | The development is on a lot having an area 0 m2 to 2,999 m2 | Circumstance (C): If a shade sail or an ‘open carport’, the shade sail or ‘open carport’ may have a road frontage setback that is less than the setback specified in Circumstance (A) or Circumstance (B) only if it complies with the following: (a) no more than one (1) shade sail or open carport per lot is non-compliant with the setbacks specified in Circumstance (A) or Circumstance (B); (b) the shade sail or open carport is not located within a nine (9) by nine (9) metre truncation at the corner of two road frontages (refer to Figure SC10.1.5); (c) the height of the shade sail or open carport does not exceed 3.5 metres above ground level to the apex; (d) the maximum width is the lesser of seven (7) metres or fifty (50) per centum of the width of the road frontage from which vehicle access is obtained (measured from the inside of the outermost supporting posts); (e) supporting posts have a setback of at least one (1) metre from any road frontage lot boundary; (f) there are zero enclosing or screening elements (for example, doors, walls, windows, screens or similar) along any line of supports of that part of the shade sail or open carport which does not comply with the setback specified in Circumstance (A) or Circumstance (B); and (g) the sum perimeter dimension of supports located within the setback does not exceed fifteen (15) per centum of the total perimeter dimension (along the line of supports) of that part of the shade sail or carport within the same setback (refer to Figure SC10.1.7).$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$Rural zone code p.P6-89 (PDF p.8); Emerging community zone code p.P6-76 (PDF p.6); Schedule 10 p.SC10-2 to SC10-5 (PDF pp.2-5)$q$, NULL, $q$Rural zone code / Emerging community zone code + Schedule 10$q$, NULL, $q$https://www.livingstone.qld.gov.au/files/sharedassets/public/v/1/doing-business/documents/10_Sch10_Boundary_setbacks_for_zones_V4_Adopted_2025_02_18.pdf$q$, $q$SC1.2 Setback: "the shortest distance, measured horizontally, between the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the boundary of the lot where the building or structure is." Outermost projection excludes a retractable blind, fixed screen, rainwater fitting or ornamental attachment. Outermost projection height is measured to ground level directly below that point.$q$, $q$lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_open_carport$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_open_carport", "instrument_version": "LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02", "topic": "SETBACK.FRONTAGE", "title": "Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Road Frontage Boundaries Circumstance (C)", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_FRONT", "operator": ">=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || Table SC10.1.1: Setback standards for development located in the Rural Zone or the Emerging Community Zone | Note: The setback standards for the Emerging Community Zone apply where located in an area that is not the subject of a Local Plan, or an approved structure plan area, which has approved documents that vary the effect of the planning scheme with alternative assessment benchmarks for setbacks. | The development is on a lot having an area 0 m2 to 2,999 m2 | Circumstance (C): If a shade sail or an ‘open carport’, the shade sail or ‘open carport’ may have a road frontage setback that is less than the setback specified in Circumstance (A) or Circumstance (B) only if it complies with the following: (a) no more than one (1) shade sail or open carport per lot is non-compliant with the setbacks specified in Circumstance (A) or Circumstance (B); (b) the shade sail or open carport is not located within a nine (9) by nine (9) metre truncation at the corner of two road frontages (refer to Figure SC10.1.5); (c) the height of the shade sail or open carport does not exceed 3.5 metres above ground level to the apex; (d) the maximum width is the lesser of seven (7) metres or fifty (50) per centum of the width of the road frontage from which vehicle access is obtained (measured from the inside of the outermost supporting posts); (e) supporting posts have a setback of at least one (1) metre from any road frontage lot boundary; (f) there are zero enclosing or screening elements (for example, doors, walls, windows, screens or similar) along any line of supports of that part of the shade sail or open carport which does not comply with the setback specified in Circumstance (A) or Circumstance (B); and (g) the sum perimeter dimension of supports located within the setback does not exceed fifteen (15) per centum of the total perimeter dimension (along the line of supports) of that part of the shade sail or carport within the same setback (refer to Figure SC10.1.7).", "extracted_value": 1, "extracted_operator": "conditional"}, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2025-05-02", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "LIVINGSTONE"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:RURAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:EMERGING_COMMUNITY"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_10A"], "sources": [{"key": "lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_open_carport", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"no more than one non-compliant shade sail or open carport per lot\", \"not within 9 m x 9 m corner truncation\", \"height <= 3.5 m to apex\", \"width <= lesser of 7 m or 50% of the road frontage width from which vehicle access is obtained\", \"supporting posts setback >= 1 m from any road frontage lot boundary\", \"no enclosing or screening elements along any line of supports within the setback\", \"supports within setback <= 15% of perimeter (Figure SC10.1.7)\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": null, \"parameter\": \"road frontage setback of supporting posts of a shade sail or open carport that does not meet Circumstance (A)/(B)\", \"operator\": \"conditional\", \"value\": 1}\nLot conditions (not encoded): lots 0 m2 to 2,999 m2\nStructure scope 'shade sail or 'open carport'' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - Part 1 s1.6(3): \"This planning scheme, through Part 5, regulates building work in accordance with sections 32 and 33 of the Building Act 1975.\" and s1.6(4)(c) lists \"Relevant zone codes\" (and (e) \"Seaspray Local Plan\") as building assessment provisions; the s1.6 editor's note cites \"alternative boundary clearances and site cover provisions for Class 1 and 10 structures under section 33\". Table 5.6.1 makes standalone Class 10a building work accepted subject to requirements against these AOs.\nResearcher notes: 'Open carport' defined in SC1.2 (two or more sides open, not less than one-third of perimeter open). For the Emerging Community Zone the table applies only outside a Local Plan or approved structure plan area (table note). In the Rural Zone, AO5.1 applies in all areas excluding the Yaamba Historic Township Precinct (see lsc_rur_yaamba_* rules)."}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_open_carport@2025-05-02$q$;
INSERT INTO rule_relationships (from_rule_version_id, to_rule_id, type, basis_provision_id, verification, notes) VALUES ($q$LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_open_carport@2025-05-02$q$, $q$QDC12.A1a.ROAD_SETBACK$q$, 'OVERRIDES', p('QLD_BUILDING_ACT_1975@2026-02-01', 's 33'), 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', 'Alternative provision (Building Act s33(4)): QDC applies only to the extent this provision does not. Scope must be confirmed per rule (zone/precinct/structure).');
INSERT INTO rule_relationships (from_rule_version_id, to_rule_id, type, basis_provision_id, verification, notes) VALUES ($q$LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_front_open_carport@2025-05-02$q$, $q$QDC11.A1a.FRONTAGE_SETBACK$q$, 'OVERRIDES', p('QLD_BUILDING_ACT_1975@2026-02-01', 's 33'), 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', 'Alternative provision (Building Act s33(4)): QDC applies only to the extent this provision does not. Scope must be confirmed per rule (zone/precinct/structure).');
SELECT define_provision($q$LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02$q$, $q$Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Side and Rear Boundaries Circumstance (A); Table SC10.1.9$q$, 'TABLE', $q$AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || Table SC10.1.1: Setback standards for development located in the Rural Zone or the Emerging Community Zone | Note: The setback standards for the Emerging Community Zone apply where located in an area that is not the subject of a Local Plan, or an approved structure plan area, which has approved documents that vary the effect of the planning scheme with alternative assessment benchmarks for setbacks. | The development is on a lot having an area 0 m2 to 2,999 m2 | The side and rear setbacks identified in Circumstance (A) or Circumstance (B) apply to buildings or structures unless the building or structure complies with Circumstance (C), or Circumstance (D), or Circumstance (E), or Circumstance (F). | Circumstance (A): If the lot is rectangular or near rectangular with a road frontage of fifteen (15) metres or less, the setback for the building or structure is in accordance with Table SC10.1.9. || Table SC10.1.9: Side and rear lot boundary setbacks where lot road frontages are fifteen metres or less | Road Frontage (in metres) | Side and Rear Boundary Setback (in metres) | At any point where the ‘outermost projection height’ is between 2 metres and 4.5 metres | At any point where the ‘outermost projection height’ is 4.501 metres to 7.5 metres | At any point where the ‘outermost projection height’ is greater than 7.5 metres || 14.501 – 15.000 | 1.425 | 1.900 || 14.001 – 14.500 | 1.350 | 1.800 || 13.501 – 14.000 | 1.275 | 1.700 || 13.001 – 13.500 | 1.200 | 1.600 || 12.501 – 13.000 | 1.125 | 1.500 || 12.001 – 12.500 | 1.050 | 1.400 || 11.501 – 12.000 | 0.975 | 1.300 || 11.001 – 11.500 | 0.900 | 1.200 || 10.501 – 11.000 | 0.825 | 1.100 || 10.500 or less | 0.750 | 1.000 || 2 metres plus 0.5 of a metre for every 3 metres or part of 3 metres by which the height exceeds 7.5 metres.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$Rural zone code p.P6-89 (PDF p.8); Emerging community zone code p.P6-76 (PDF p.6); Schedule 10 p.SC10-2 to SC10-3 (PDF pp.2-3); Tables SC10.1.9/SC10.1.10 at SC10-21 (PDF p.21)$q$, NULL, $q$Rural zone code / Emerging community zone code + Schedule 10$q$, NULL, $q$https://www.livingstone.qld.gov.au/files/sharedassets/public/v/1/doing-business/documents/10_Sch10_Boundary_setbacks_for_zones_V4_Adopted_2025_02_18.pdf$q$, $q$SC1.2 Setback: "the shortest distance, measured horizontally, between the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the boundary of the lot where the building or structure is." Outermost projection excludes a retractable blind, fixed screen, rainwater fitting or ornamental attachment. Outermost projection height is measured to ground level directly below that point.$q$, $q$lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_side_rear_frontage_le15$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_side_rear_frontage_le15", "instrument_version": "LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02", "topic": "SETBACK.SIDE", "title": "Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Side and Rear Boundaries Circumstance (A); Table SC10.1.9", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "TABLE", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_SIDE", "operator": ">=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "OPH > 7.5 m: 2 + 0.5 * ceil((OPH - 7.5)/3)", "extracted_value": null, "extracted_operator": "conditional"}, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2025-05-02", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "LIVINGSTONE"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:RURAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:EMERGING_COMMUNITY"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_side_rear_frontage_le15", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"applies to side AND rear boundaries\", \"measured at any point by outermost projection height\", \"road frontage 14.501–15.000 m: OPH 2–4.5 m: 1.425 m; OPH 4.501–7.5 m: 1.900 m\", \"road frontage 14.001–14.500 m: OPH 2–4.5 m: 1.350 m; OPH 4.501–7.5 m: 1.800 m\", \"road frontage 13.501–14.000 m: OPH 2–4.5 m: 1.275 m; OPH 4.501–7.5 m: 1.700 m\", \"road frontage 13.001–13.500 m: OPH 2–4.5 m: 1.200 m; OPH 4.501–7.5 m: 1.600 m\", \"road frontage 12.501–13.000 m: OPH 2–4.5 m: 1.125 m; OPH 4.501–7.5 m: 1.500 m\", \"road frontage 12.001–12.500 m: OPH 2–4.5 m: 1.050 m; OPH 4.501–7.5 m: 1.400 m\", \"road frontage 11.501–12.000 m: OPH 2–4.5 m: 0.975 m; OPH 4.501–7.5 m: 1.300 m\", \"road frontage 11.001–11.500 m: OPH 2–4.5 m: 0.900 m; OPH 4.501–7.5 m: 1.200 m\", \"road frontage 10.501–11.000 m: OPH 2–4.5 m: 0.825 m; OPH 4.501–7.5 m: 1.100 m\", \"road frontage 10.500 m or less: OPH 2–4.5 m: 0.750 m; OPH 4.501–7.5 m: 1.000 m\", \"OPH > 7.5 m (any frontage <= 15 m): 2 m + 0.5 m for every 3 m or part of 3 m by which height exceeds 7.5 m\"], \"exceptions\": [\"Class 10a building or part may be within the setback - see Circumstance (C) rule\", \"rainwater tank (incl. stand) <= 2.4 m high (Circumstance (D)(a))\", \"ornamental/horticultural pergola or structure <= 2.4 m, unenclosed (Circumstance (D)(b))\", \"building or structure (or combination such as fence + retaining wall) not exceeding 2 m outermost projection height / combined height (Circumstance (F))\"], \"formula_text\": \"OPH > 7.5 m: 2 + 0.5 * ceil((OPH - 7.5)/3)\", \"parameter\": \"side and rear boundary setback by road frontage width and outermost projection height (OPH)\", \"operator\": \"conditional\", \"value\": null}\nLot conditions (not encoded): lots 0 m2 to 2,999 m2; rectangular or near rectangular lot with road frontage <= 15 m\nStructure scope 'buildings or structures (a part of the building or structure)' mapped by keyword to ['ANY']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - Part 1 s1.6(3): \"This planning scheme, through Part 5, regulates building work in accordance with sections 32 and 33 of the Building Act 1975.\" and s1.6(4)(c) lists \"Relevant zone codes\" (and (e) \"Seaspray Local Plan\") as building assessment provisions; the s1.6 editor's note cites \"alternative boundary clearances and site cover provisions for Class 1 and 10 structures under section 33\". Table 5.6.1 makes standalone Class 10a building work accepted subject to requirements against these AOs.\nResearcher notes: Table SC10.1.9 values transcribed from pdftotext -layout output of the official PDF (rows read left-to-right); the >7.5 m column is a single merged cell spanning all rows. Structures below 2 m OPH are effectively unregulated (table starts at 2 m and Circumstance (F) exempts them). For the Emerging Community Zone the table applies only outside a Local Plan or approved structure plan area (table note). In the Rural Zone, AO5.1 applies in all areas excluding the Yaamba Historic Township Precinct (see lsc_rur_yaamba_* rules)."}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_side_rear_frontage_le15@2025-05-02$q$;
