SELECT define_provision($q$LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02$q$, $q$Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Side and Rear Boundaries Circumstance (B); Table SC10.1.10$q$, 'TABLE', $q$AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || Table SC10.1.1: Setback standards for development located in the Rural Zone or the Emerging Community Zone | Note: The setback standards for the Emerging Community Zone apply where located in an area that is not the subject of a Local Plan, or an approved structure plan area, which has approved documents that vary the effect of the planning scheme with alternative assessment benchmarks for setbacks. | The development is on a lot having an area 0 m2 to 2,999 m2 | The side and rear setbacks identified in Circumstance (A) or Circumstance (B) apply to buildings or structures unless the building or structure complies with Circumstance (C), or Circumstance (D), or Circumstance (E), or Circumstance (F). | Circumstance (B): If the lot has a road frontage greater than fifteen (15) metres, the setback for the building or structure is in accordance with Table SC10.1.10. || Table SC10.1.10: Side and rear lot boundary setbacks where lot road frontages are greater than fifteen metres | Road Frontage (in metres) | Side and Rear Boundary Setback (in metres) | At any point where the ‘outermost projection height’ is between 2 metres and 4.5 metres | At any point where the ‘outermost projection height’ is 4.501 metres to 7.5 metres | At any point where the ‘outermost projection height’ is greater than 7.5 metres || 15.001 or greater | 1.5 metres | 2 metres | 2 metres plus 0.5 of a metre for every 3 metres or part of 3 metres by which the height exceeds 7.5 metres.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$Rural zone code p.P6-89 (PDF p.8); Emerging community zone code p.P6-76 (PDF p.6); Schedule 10 p.SC10-2 to SC10-3 (PDF pp.2-3); Tables SC10.1.9/SC10.1.10 at SC10-21 (PDF p.21)$q$, NULL, $q$Rural zone code / Emerging community zone code + Schedule 10$q$, NULL, $q$https://www.livingstone.qld.gov.au/files/sharedassets/public/v/1/doing-business/documents/10_Sch10_Boundary_setbacks_for_zones_V4_Adopted_2025_02_18.pdf$q$, $q$SC1.2 Setback: "the shortest distance, measured horizontally, between the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the boundary of the lot where the building or structure is." Outermost projection excludes a retractable blind, fixed screen, rainwater fitting or ornamental attachment. Outermost projection height is measured to ground level directly below that point.$q$, $q$lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_side_rear_frontage_gt15$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "LSC.lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_side_rear_frontage_gt15", "instrument_version": "LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02", "topic": "SETBACK.SIDE", "title": "Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Side and Rear Boundaries Circumstance (B); Table SC10.1.10", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "TABLE", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_SIDE", "operator": ">=", "value": 1.5, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2025-05-02", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "LIVINGSTONE"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:RURAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:EMERGING_COMMUNITY"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "lsc_rur_ec_lt3000_side_rear_frontage_gt15", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"applies to side AND rear boundaries\", \"OPH 2 m to 4.5 m: 1.5 m\", \"OPH 4.501 m to 7.5 m: 2 m\", \"OPH > 7.5 m: 2 m plus 0.5 m for every 3 m or part of 3 m by which height exceeds 7.5 m\"], \"exceptions\": [\"Class 10a building or part may be within the setback - see Circumstance (C) rule\", \"rainwater tank (incl. stand) <= 2.4 m high (Circumstance (D)(a))\", \"ornamental/horticultural pergola or structure <= 2.4 m, unenclosed (Circumstance (D)(b))\", \"building or structure (or combination such as fence + retaining wall) not exceeding 2 m outermost projection height / combined height (Circumstance (F))\"], \"formula_text\": \"OPH > 7.5 m: 2 + 0.5 * ceil((OPH - 7.5)/3)\", \"parameter\": \"side and rear boundary setback by outermost projection height (OPH)\", \"operator\": \">=\", \"value\": 1.5}\nLot conditions (not encoded): lots 0 m2 to 2,999 m2; road frontage > 15 m\nStructure scope 'buildings or structures (a part of the building or structure)' mapped by keyword to ['ANY']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - Part 1 s1.6(3): \"This planning scheme, through Part 5, regulates building work in accordance with sections 32 and 33 of the Building Act 1975.\" and s1.6(4)(c) lists \"Relevant zone codes\" (and (e) \"Seaspray Local Plan\") as building assessment provisions; the s1.6 editor's note cites \"alternative boundary clearances and site cover provisions for Class 1 and 10 structures under section 33\". Table 5.6.1 makes standalone Class 10a building work accepted subject to requirements against these AOs.\nResearcher notes: Value 1.5 m is the minimum (OPH 2-4.5 m band). For the Emerging Community Zone the table applies only outside a Local Plan or approved structure plan area (table note). In the Rural Zone, AO5.1 applies in all areas excluding the Yaamba Historic Township Precinct (see lsc_rur_yaamba_* rules)."}$q$::jsonb);
