SELECT define_provision($q$LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02$q$, $q$Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Side and Rear Boundaries$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || AO5.1 Buildings or structures have a setback from side, rear and road frontage lot boundaries in compliance with the setback standards identified in Table SC10.1.1 of Schedule 10. || Table SC10.1.1: Setback standards for development located in the Rural Zone or the Emerging Community Zone | Note: The setback standards for the Emerging Community Zone apply where located in an area that is not the subject of a Local Plan, or an approved structure plan area, which has approved documents that vary the effect of the planning scheme with alternative assessment benchmarks for setbacks. | The development is on a lot having an area from 10,000 m2 to 49,999 m2 (i.e. the lot has an area from 1 Ha to 4.9999 Ha) | The side and rear setbacks identified in Circumstance (A) apply to buildings or structures unless the building or structure complies with Circumstance (B). | Circumstance (A): Buildings or structures have a setback from side and rear boundaries in accordance with the following: | (b) if a non-habitable building or structure, the greater of the following: (i) a setback of at least ten (10) metres; or (ii) a distance equal to the ‘outermost projection height’ of the building or structure. | Circumstance (B): A building or structure that does not have an ‘outermost projection height’ exceeding two (2) metres.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$Rural zone code p.P6-89 (PDF p.8); Emerging community zone code p.P6-76 (PDF p.6); Schedule 10 p.SC10-5 to SC10-6 (PDF pp.5-6)$q$, NULL, $q$Rural zone code / Emerging community zone code + Schedule 10$q$, NULL, $q$https://www.livingstone.qld.gov.au/files/sharedassets/public/v/1/doing-business/documents/10_Sch10_Boundary_setbacks_for_zones_V4_Adopted_2025_02_18.pdf$q$, $q$SC1.2 Setback: "the shortest distance, measured horizontally, between the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the boundary of the lot where the building or structure is." Outermost projection excludes a retractable blind, fixed screen, rainwater fitting or ornamental attachment. Outermost projection height is measured to ground level directly below that point.$q$, $q$lsc_rur_ec_1ha_5ha_side_rear$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "LSC.lsc_rur_ec_1ha_5ha_side_rear", "instrument_version": "LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02", "topic": "SETBACK.SIDE", "title": "Rural zone code Table 6.5.4.4.1 AO5.1; Emerging community zone code Table 6.5.2.4.1 AO5.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.1 Side and Rear Boundaries", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_SIDE", "operator": ">=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "max(10, OPH)", "extracted_value": 10, "extracted_operator": "conditional"}, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2025-05-02", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "LIVINGSTONE"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:RURAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:EMERGING_COMMUNITY"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_10A"], "sources": [{"key": "lsc_rur_ec_1ha_5ha_side_rear", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"applies to side AND rear boundaries\", \"non-habitable building or structure: greater of 10 m or a distance equal to its outermost projection height\"], \"exceptions\": [\"building or structure not exceeding 2 m outermost projection height\"], \"formula_text\": \"max(10, OPH)\", \"parameter\": \"side and rear boundary setback\", \"operator\": \"conditional\", \"value\": 10}\nLot conditions (not encoded): lots 10,000 m2 to 49,999 m2 (1 ha to 4.9999 ha)\nStructure scope 'a non-habitable building or structure' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - Part 1 s1.6(3): \"This planning scheme, through Part 5, regulates building work in accordance with sections 32 and 33 of the Building Act 1975.\" and s1.6(4)(c) lists \"Relevant zone codes\" (and (e) \"Seaspray Local Plan\") as building assessment provisions; the s1.6 editor's note cites \"alternative boundary clearances and site cover provisions for Class 1 and 10 structures under section 33\". Table 5.6.1 makes standalone Class 10a building work accepted subject to requirements against these AOs.\nResearcher notes: Habitable accommodation buildings limb (a) omitted (out of scope). For the Emerging Community Zone the table applies only outside a Local Plan or approved structure plan area. In the Rural Zone AO5.1 applies everywhere except the Yaamba Historic Township Precinct."}$q$::jsonb);
