SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "LSC.lsc_rr_ge1ha_side_rear", "instrument_version": "LSC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2018@2025-05-02", "topic": "SETBACK.SIDE", "title": "Rural residential zone code Table 6.5.5.4.1 AO3.1; Schedule 10 Table SC10.1.4 Side and Rear Boundaries", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_SIDE", "operator": ">=", "value": 10, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2025-05-02", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "LIVINGSTONE"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LSC:RURAL_RESIDENTIAL"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "lsc_rr_ge1ha_side_rear", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"applies to side AND rear boundaries\"], \"exceptions\": [\"building or structure (or combination e.g. fence + retaining wall) not exceeding 2 m outermost projection height / combined height\"], \"formula_text\": null, \"parameter\": \"side and rear boundary setback\", \"operator\": \">=\", \"value\": 10}\nLot conditions (not encoded): not in Park Residential Precinct; lots >= 10,000 m2 (>= 1 ha)\nStructure scope 'buildings or structures' mapped by keyword to ['ANY']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - Part 1 s1.6(3): \"This planning scheme, through Part 5, regulates building work in accordance with sections 32 and 33 of the Building Act 1975.\" and s1.6(4)(c) lists \"Relevant zone codes\" (and (e) \"Seaspray Local Plan\") as building assessment provisions; the s1.6 editor's note cites \"alternative boundary clearances and site cover provisions for Class 1 and 10 structures under section 33\". Table 5.6.1 makes standalone Class 10a building work accepted subject to requirements against these AOs.\nResearcher notes: No Class 10a concession (unlike urban tables); applies equally to dwellings and outbuildings."}$q$::jsonb);
